---
import Guide from '../layouts/Guide.astro';
import { pick } from '../data/faq';
---
<Guide
  page="stream"
  lede="See who is watching on Jellyfin and Plex, and why a stream is transcoding. Pause, stop or message a session from your phone. You still watch in Jellyfin or Plex."
  services={['jellyfin', 'plex']}
  questions={pick('player', 'account', 'certs')}
  related={['seerr', 'homelab', 'install']}
>
  <h2>Who is watching</h2>
  <p>Each session shows the title, the person, the device and how far in they are. You also see whether it plays directly or transcodes, and why. The list stays live while you look at it.</p>

  <h2>What you can do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Jellyfin</strong>: pause, stop or message a session; libraries, users, devices, resume points and scheduled tasks.</li>
    <li><strong>Plex</strong>: stop a session with a message the viewer sees; libraries, on deck, devices and playlists.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Part of everything else</h2>
  <p>Discover's search includes Jellyfin and Plex, so a title's page says if you already have it. Home can show what you were halfway through.</p>

  <h2>Signing in</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Jellyfin</strong> takes an API key, then asks whose watch history to show. Family members can sign in as themselves.</li>
    <li><strong>Plex</strong> takes a token, which already belongs to a user.</li>
  </ul>
</Guide>
